.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt QUOTAON 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm quotaon ,
.Nm quotaoff
.Nd turn file system quotas on and off
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl g
.Op Fl u
.Op Fl v
.Fl a | Ar filesystem ...
.Nm quotaoff
.Op Fl g
.Op Fl u
.Op Fl v
.Fl a | Ar filesystem ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
tells the kernel to enforce the user or group limits of a volume, read
from
.Pa .quota.user
or
.Pa .quota.group
at its root, which
.Xr quotacheck 8
makes.
.Nm quotaoff
stops it.
A volume wants quotas when
.Pa .quota.ops.user
or
.Pa .quota.ops.group
is at its root.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Every mounted local volume, for the types it wants.
.It Fl g
Group quotas only.
.It Fl u
User quotas only.
.It Fl v
Say what was done.
.El
.Pp
Without
.Fl g
or
.Fl u ,
the types the volume wants; with them, those types, even if it does not.
A
.Ar filesystem
is any path on the volume.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width .quota.ops.group -compact
.It Pa .quota.user
.It Pa .quota.group
the quota files, at the volume's root
.It Pa .quota.ops.user
.It Pa .quota.ops.group
the volume wants that type of quota
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr quota 1 ,
.Xr quotactl 2 ,
.Xr edquota 8 ,
.Xr quotacheck 8 ,
.Xr repquota 8
.Sh HISTORY
Minkar's
.Nm
is its own.
